# What each level chooses that is not a stage: the lines stage 4 and stage 12
# read through level_choice (generated into copal-prep.sh by 'make
# sync-playbooks'). One level per line:
#
#   level|browser|withhold
#
# browser   the graphical browser stage 4 installs when nobody is at the
#           keyboard: brave, firefox-esr, chromium or badwolf. Brave only
#           where Flathub publishes it (x86_64, aarch64); anywhere else
#           stage 4 takes badwolf, whatever this says.
# withhold  graphical browsers stage 12's 'everything' leaves out at this
#           level, space-separated: at full, three more engines beside
#           Brave and Firefox ESR are only card and menu clutter.
#
# The terminal and the file manager are not here: they are chosen by the
# session (foot first on Wayland, urxvt on X) and by what is installed, not
# by level, in stage 4's desktop helpers.
server|badwolf|
medium|badwolf|
full|brave|dillo netsurf badwolf
